[Music]  nestled in the countryside this baroque  palace was only recently returned to its  former glory  known as a favorite of the empress  elizabeth of austria the queen of  hungary this is one palace truly built  for a royal family  but today it's open to visitors from  everywhere  this great big story was made possible  by  budapest  spice of europe  [Music]  considered hungary's answer to the  palace of versailles this masterpiece of  baroque architecture has everything  you'd want in a palace  the royal palace of godula was completed  in 1748 and was given as a wedding gift  to the new queen and king of hungary  the palace has a double u-shape and is  surrounded by an enormous park  [Music]  the ceremonial hall forms the center of  the palace's symmetrical plan  at the far end of the castle is a church  renovated in 1749.  a baroque theater hosted productions for  hungary's aristocracy  many of the mechanisms for changing  scenery still work today  in 1867 the hungarian parliament  purchased the palace and offered the  castle as a coronation gift to franz  joseph king of hungary and emperor of  austria  empress elizabeth of austria the queen  of hungary known more colloquially as  cece was particularly fond of the palace  of godullah and bathed the walls in her  favorite color violet blue  cece played a vital role balancing power  between austria and hungary  she loved hungary and its people and  devoted herself to learning the  hungarian language  though the connected rooms didn't offer  much in terms of privacy they were a  marked improvement from the busy  viennese royal court  the palace features walls and ceilings  decorated in a classical baroque style  the palace garden features tree-lined  avenues and a diverse collection of  beautiful flowers and plant life  both inside and out the palace of  godella is truly fit for a queen  [Music]

